AV1 OBU writer vendored from GStreamer
======================================
gstav1bitwriter.h and gstav1parser.h are copied unmodified (apart from their #include lines, which now point at
gstcompat.h) from GStreamer 1.28.2; gstav1bitwriter.c carries three marked "rockchip-vaapi" changes (below) and is
otherwise unmodified. Source:, subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/codecparsers/.
Copyright (C) 2022 Intel Corporation; licence LGPL-2.0-or-later (see the file headers). gstcompat.h/.c supply the small
subset of GLib and GstBitWriter they need, so no GLib or GStreamer is linked.

Why: rockchip-vaapi must hand Rockchip MPP a complete AV1 OBU stream, but VA-API clients deliver only parsed
parameters and tile payloads, so the sequence and frame headers are regenerated from VADecPictureParameterBufferAV1
(see docs and the av1-research notes). Round trip verified 2026-10-11: every sequence and frame header of four
SVT-AV1 test streams (8-bit, 10-bit, film grain) re-written bit-exactly.

Changes to gstav1bitwriter.c (all marked with a "rockchip-vaapi" comment):
1. segmentation_params() implemented per spec 5.9.14 — the GStreamer copy refused frames with segmentation
   (common in libaom/YouTube encodes).
2. loop_filter_params(): the update_ref_delta / update_mode_delta bits are always written. GStreamer compared each
   value with the spec default; a VA-API driver only knows the effective values and the decoder keeps the primary
   reference's deltas for entries not updated, so every entry must be written.
3. global_motion_params(): PrevGmParams was copied from the address of ref_global_motion_params (whose first
   members are the is_global flags) instead of its gm_params array, so deltas were coded against garbage whenever
   primary_ref_frame != NONE. Upstream bug (GStreamer gst-plugins-bad, gstav1bitwriter.c); report after release.
Verified 2026-10-11 on the Orange Pi 5B: every sequence and frame header of seven test streams (SVT-AV1 and libaom;
8/10-bit, film grain, segmentation, 2x2 tiles, error-resilient, global motion) re-written bit-exactly, and the
re-serialised streams decode bit-exactly through MPP (tests/av1).

Update: fetch the three files from the GStreamer tag you want, re-apply the include edits, rebuild, re-run the round
trip test (tests/av1rt).
